---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "Trim"
letter: "T"
anchor: "trim"
category: "edibles"
---

The leaves removed from cannabis buds during the trimming process after harvest. Sugar leaves (small leaves growing directly from buds) are covered in trichomes and have meaningful cannabinoid content. Fan leaves (larger leaves from the main stem and branches) have very low cannabinoid content. Sugar leaf trim is excellent for edibles and infusions — use more of it than you would flower to achieve equivalent potency.
